From 92f8fc631aa2b6fdc59ad5a7db2194f2e3fc8826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 17:47:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: add Spotify Now Playing mode with album artwork

New home-menu activity that shows dithered album art, track/artist and a
progress bar for the user's current Spotify playback (Web API observer
only - no audio).

- lib/Spotify: PKCE auth helpers (host-tested), currently-playing JSON
  parser using a filtered ArduinoJson document (host-tested), Web API
  client modeled on KOReaderSyncClient (small TLS buffers + heap guard),
  SD-card store with device-bound token obfuscation
- src/network/SpotifyAuthServer: minimal HTTP server for the QR-driven
  one-time setup and OAuth PKCE login/callback routes; only runs during
  setup, separate from the file-transfer server
- src/activities/network/SpotifyActivity: WiFi bring-up via
  WifiSelectionActivity, 10s/30s adaptive polling, art downloaded once
  per album and converted to a 1-bit Atkinson-dithered BMP at display
  size, FAST_REFRESH progress ticks with periodic HALF_REFRESH de-ghost
- docs/spotify.md + docs/spotify-redirect.html: setup guide and an HTTPS
  bridge page for Spotify's https-only redirect URI policy
- 12 new host unit tests (spotify_auth, spotify_parser)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017CwTd5jjLANup3CKUBJ1BS
