From ab7ce09385ef93bde958a975f7fcaaae7df56359 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 19:08:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: desktop simulator support + fixes found by running
 the mode

Ran the Spotify mode end-to-end in the crosspoint-simulator (native SDL2
build) and fixed everything it surfaced:

- platformio.ini: add [env:simulator] per the simulator's Linux sample,
  plus -Isim_support/include for an esp_random.h shim the simulator does
  not ship yet
- SpotifyActivity.h: include SpotifyAuthServer.h instead of a forward
  declaration - unique_ptr member destruction in other TUs (and the
  ctor unwind path) needs the complete type; caught at native compile,
  would also have broken the device build
- SpotifyAuthServer: deserializeJson needs an lvalue String body (same
  pattern as CrossPointWebServer)
- SpotifyClient: use the mbedtls_sha256 context API - the common subset
  between device mbedTLS and the simulator shim
- SpotifyStore: accept a plaintext refresh_token with obfuscated resave
  (mirrors PersistableStoreBase::extractPassword), enabling seeded sim
  demos and hand-recovery
- Now Playing: draw the progress bar directly - GUI.drawProgressBar
  appends a percentage label that collided with the time readout
- home menu: proper 32x32 music-note icon (new UIIcon::Music, mapped in
  LyraTheme) instead of the icon-less entry
- sim_support/spotify-demo/: mock API fixtures + sample art for
  CROSSPOINT_SIM_HTTP_MOCK_ROOT demos; docs/spotify.md documents the
  simulator workflow

Verified: pio run -e simulator builds clean; driven headlessly under
Xvfb through home -> WiFi -> now-playing/paused/nothing-playing/link
screens; all 97 host tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017CwTd5jjLANup3CKUBJ1BS
